# Engine Research Findings

Meridian's engine is assembled from LGPL-licensed CX Wine components + open-source rendering layers (DXMT, DXVK, MoltenVK) + Apple's freely-distributed GPTK. `release-engine.sh` copies these from CrossOver Preview into a self-contained engine tarball. End users never need CrossOver installed. This document records architecture decisions and CLI-verified findings so future sessions can build on them.

---

## Engine: CX Wine 11.4 (CrossOver Preview) — Current

**Current Meridian engine:** CX Wine 11.4 from CrossOver Preview.
**Previous:** Gcenx Wine 11.6 — tried April 2026, broke TLS on macOS 26 (see below). Reverted.
**Before that:** CX Wine 11.4 — the original working engine.
**Before that:** Wine 8.0.1 (CrossOverFOSS 23.7.1) — obsolete.

**Why CX Wine over Gcenx Wine (TLS failure, CLI-verified April 2026):**
Gcenx Wine 11.6 fails HTTPS connections on macOS 26.4 with HTTP error 0 on Steam CDN.
steam.exe bootstrap_log.txt: `Download failed: http error 0 (cdn.steamstatic.com/...)` →
`Error: Steam needs to be online to update.` on every attempt. Root cause unknown — possibly
a macOS 26-specific Security.framework incompatibility with Gcenx Wine's standalone TLS path.
CX Wine 11.4 bootstraps correctly: CLI-verified April 2026 at 130 MB/s download speed.

**Confirmed FALSE theory (do not repeat):**
Earlier hypothesis was that CX Wine uses GnuTLS via `lib64/libgnutls.30.dylib` and fails
standalone. This is WRONG. `otool -L crypt32.so` on BOTH CX Wine and Gcenx Wine shows:
`/System/Library/Frameworks/Security.framework` — neither links to libgnutls. The TLS
failure with Gcenx Wine is NOT caused by libgnutls; it's a Gcenx Wine incompatibility with
macOS 26. CX Wine TLS works fine standalone when lib64 is NOT on DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH.

**CRITICAL: lib64 must NOT be on DYLD at runtime (but for different reason than thought):**
lib64 contains libgnutls.30.dylib. Even though crypt32.so doesn't LINK to it, dynamic
loading via dlopen could still pick it up. The app's steamCMDEnvironment and environment(for:)
only add `lib:lib/wine/x86_64-unix` to DYLD — never lib64. This is correct and must stay.

**Why CX Wine also enables GPTK (D3D12):**
CX Wine has `ntdll.__wine_unix_call` (a CodeWeavers extension). GPTK's d3d12.dll and dxgi.dll
both import this function. WineEngine.detect() does a binary string search for
`__wine_unix_call\0` in ntdll.so — if found, gptkPath is set and GPTK env vars are injected
for game launches. With CX Wine: gptkPath set → D3D12 → D3DMetal → Metal works.
With Gcenx Wine: no `__wine_unix_call` → gptkPath = nil → D3D12 disabled.

**Why CX Wine 11.4 has all the same DX11 patches as Gcenx 11.6:**

| Issue | Wine 8.0.1 | Wine 11.5 |
|---|---|---|
| `IsMouseInPointerEnabled` | MISSING → Unity crash | Properly exported |
| win32u.dll abort stubs | **926** | **0** |
| user32.dll exports | 782 | 831 (+49) |
| wiremac.so Metal APIs | Missing | Present |
| DXMT compatibility | Broken | Works |
| steam.exe bootstrap | Crash-loops | Bootstraps correctly |

