## Rendering Stack: DXMT (D3D11 → Metal)

### What DXMT Is

DXMT (3Shain/dxmt) translates DirectX 11 and DirectX 10 calls to Apple Metal. It is the primary renderer for DX11 games on macOS.

### DXMT Layout in Meridian Engine (builtin mode)

```
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d11.dll     (DXMT PE shim, ~5MB)
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/dxgi.dll      (DXMT DXGI)
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d10core.dll (DXMT D3D10)
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/wiremetal.dll (DXMT Metal PE stub)
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-unix/wiremetal.so     (DXMT Metal bridge, ~33MB, includes LLVM/AIR compiler)
wine/lib/wine/i386-windows/*.dll           (32-bit variants)
```

**Builtin mode:** DLLs live alongside Wine's own DLLs in `lib/wine/x86_64-windows/`. Wine loads them automatically as builtins — no `WINEDLLOVERRIDES` needed.

### DXMT Requirements

DXMT's `wiremetal.so` dynamically links to `wiremac.so` and requires these macOS-platform exports:
- `macdrv_view_create_metal_view`
- `macdrv_view_get_metal_layer`
- `macdrv_view_release_metal_view`
- `macdrv_create_metal_device`
- `macdrv_release_metal_device`
- `macdrv_client_surface_*` (Wine 11.x+ only)

**These were added to wiremac.so in Wine ~10.x.** This is why DXMT is completely broken with Wine 8.0.1 — the macOS graphics driver didn't export these symbols.

### DXMT + GPTK Coexistence

DXMT handles D3D11/D3D10. GPTK handles D3D12. They coexist cleanly:
- d3d11 → DXMT builtin wiremetal.so (no override needed)
- d3d12, dxgi → GPTK via WINEDLLPATH (`d3d12,dxgi=n,b`)

### DXMT Versions

- DXMT is downloaded from `3Shain/dxmt` GitHub releases
- Always use the **builtin** variant (not the "override" variant)
- DXMT must be built against a Wine version that has the `macdrv_*` Metal APIs (Wine 11.x+)
- CLI-verified March 2026: DXMT v0.74 works with Wine 11.5

