## Rendering Stack: Apple GPTK (D3D12 → D3DMetal.framework → Metal) — ACTIVE

### What GPTK Is

Apple's Game Porting Toolkit (GPTK) translates Direct3D 12 calls to Apple Metal 3 via `D3DMetal.framework`. It is the **active and only working** D3D12 path on macOS/Apple Silicon.

**Why GPTK works where VKD3D-proton fails:** GPTK bypasses Vulkan entirely. It has its own D3D12-to-Metal translator (D3DMetal.framework) and needs no Vulkan extensions. VKD3D-proton requires `VK_EXT_transform_feedback` from Vulkan — MoltenVK on Apple Silicon does not have this extension.

**Why DX12 is harder than DX11:** DX11 uses DXMT — open source, compiled against our exact Wine version, no external dependencies, no callbacks required. DX12 uses GPTK — Apple proprietary, distributed by CodeWeavers, compiled against **CrossOver Wine's internal architecture**. `libd3dshared.dylib` requires CX Wine's `NtQueryVirtualMemory(class=1000)` to register Win32 callbacks. Standard Wine 11.5 doesn't have this extension. We must reverse-engineer the interface contract entirely from `libd3dshared.dylib` disassembly.

### GPTK Architecture (Updated April 2026 — custom bridge required)

**CX's d3d12.dll cannot be used directly with Gcenx Wine.** CLI-verified April 2026: CX's d3d12.dll imports `ntdll.__wine_unix_call` (CX-specific function). Gcenx Wine only has `__wine_unix_call_dispatcher`. Loading CX's d3d12.dll produces: `wine: Call from ... to unimplemented function ntdll.dll.__wine_unix_call, aborting`. However, CX Wine + CX d3d12 was also tested and passed D3D12 init (no crash), confirming the DLLs work in their native environment.

Meridian uses a **custom d3d12 bridge** (`Scripts/build-d3d12-bridge.sh`) that uses `__wine_unix_call_dispatcher`. The bridge d3d12.so forwards to libd3dshared.dylib for D3DMetal integration.

**Bridge (Wine builtin dir):**
```
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-windows/d3d12.dll  (PE shim, uses __wine_unix_call_dispatcher via winecrt0)
wine/lib/wine/x86_64-unix/d3d12.so      (Unix adapter, promotes winemac.so, dlopen libd3dshared.dylib)
```

**GPTK framework + coordinator (lib/gptk/ — from CX Preview apple_gptk):**
```
wine/lib/gptk/external/libd3dshared.dylib  (96KB — MUST export GFXTOSInterface. A Wine artifact at ~84KB
                                             silently breaks D3D12. Validated in release-engine.sh.)
wine/lib/gptk/external/D3DMetal.framework/ (Apple Metal translator, ~63MB)
wine/lib/gptk/wine/x86_64-windows/dxgi.dll, d3d11.dll, atidxx64.dll, nvapi64.dll, nvngx.dll
wine/lib/gptk/wine/x86_64-unix/*.so        (symlinks → ../../external/libd3dshared.dylib)
```

CX's `gptk/wine/.../d3d12.dll` is REMOVED by `release-engine.sh` (replaced by bridge in `lib/wine/`). `WineEngine.detect()` checks for bridge `lib/wine/.../d3d12.dll` + `D3DMetal.framework`.

**Opcode 0 dual-purpose buffer protocol (reverse-engineered from libd3dshared.dylib disassembly):**

`WINE_UNIX_CALL(0, gGFXTDispatch)` uses the buffer as BOTH input and output in a single call.

**INPUT** — DllMain pre-populates 43 Win32 function pointers (entries 0-42). `Win32DispatchInit` does `memcpy(gWin32Dispatch, arg, 0x158)`. D3DMetal calls back through these to interact with Wine's window system.

**Complete gWin32Dispatch slot table** (reverse-engineered April 2026 from `objdump -d libd3dshared.dylib`, base address 0x91e8, each slot 8 bytes):

**CRITICAL calling convention:** `rdi` always carries the C++ wrapper object `this` pointer (context). Actual function arguments begin at `rsi` (2nd SysV register) onward. Exception: slot [28] passes the module name in `rcx` (4th register). This was confirmed by disassembling `InitSharedState_block_invoke` and `allocateBytesFromNewPages`.

