## Rendering Stack: DXVK (D3D → Vulkan → Metal via MoltenVK)

### What DXVK Is

DXVK translates DirectX 9/10/11 calls to Vulkan, which then goes through MoltenVK to Metal. It's the **fallback path** when DXMT fails (unsupported game/shader features, edge cases).

### DXVK Layout in Meridian Engine

```
wine/lib/dxvk/x86_64-windows/d3d11.dll
wine/lib/dxvk/x86_64-windows/dxgi.dll
wine/lib/dxvk/x86_64-windows/d3d10core.dll
wine/lib/dxvk/x86_64-windows/d3d9.dll
wine/lib/dxvk/x86_64-windows/d3d8.dll
```

DXVK is in a separate `lib/dxvk/` directory (not in `lib/wine/`). This is intentional: DXMT is the default (builtin), DXVK requires explicit `WINEDLLOVERRIDES=d3d11,dxgi=n,b` and WINEDLLPATH pointing to `lib/dxvk/`.

**Per-game DXVK activation:** Use `GameCompatibilityDB` to set `dxmtMode: .disabled` for games that need DXVK over DXMT.

### DXVK Source

```
Repo:  doitsujin/dxvk
Tag:   v2.7.1 (March 2026)
Asset: dxvk-2.7.1.tar.gz
```

