## CrossOver Preview 27 vs Meridian Engine Comparison

| Component | CX Preview 27 (reference only) | Meridian Engine |
|---|---|---|
| Wine version | wine-11.4 | wine-11.5 |
| user32 exports | 831 | 831 |
| win32u abort stubs | 0 | 0 |
| DXMT | `lib/dxmt/` (separate dir) | `lib/wine/` (builtin mode) |
| D3D12 | GPTK (`lib64/apple_gptk/`) | GPTK (`lib/gptk/`) |
| DXVK | `lib/dxvk/` | `lib/dxvk/` |
| MoltenVK | `lib64/libMoltenVK.dylib` | bundled with Wine |
| SteamCMD | NOT USED (runs steam.exe) | Batch mode (`+login +app_update +quit`) |
| steam.exe | Used for all installs | Bootstrap only + DRM games |

**Key architectural difference:** CX Preview runs `steam.exe` for game installs because Wine 11 is new enough that Steam actually authenticates. Meridian uses SteamCMD batch mode — this is a deliberate design choice for our no-Steam-UI architecture. When clicking Install, users never see the Steam client.

