## Game Compatibility Database

`GameCompatibilityDB.swift` stores per-game fixes. When testing a new game, add an entry documenting:
- Engine tested against
- Any crashes and their root cause
- DLL overrides needed
- DXMT mode (auto/required/disabled)
- Graphics API (dx11/dx12/vulkan)

**CLI testing methodology:**
1. Kill all Wine processes: `pkill -9 -f "meridian.app/engine"`
2. Set up env matching `WineEngine.environment(for:)` — WINEPREFIX, WINESERVER, WINELOADER, DYLD_FALLBACK_LIBRARY_PATH
3. For D3D12 games: set GPTK env vars (DYLD paths, WINEDLLPATH, WINEDLLOVERRIDES=`d3d12=b;dxgi=n,b`, CX_APPLEGPTK_LIBD3DSHARED_PATH, DYLD_FALLBACK_FRAMEWORK_PATH)
4. Run game exe directly: `wine64 "Game.exe"`
5. Observe crash messages, look for `unimplemented function`, `page fault`, or `failed to create` errors
6. Document findings in GameCompatibilityDB — classify as engine-wide or game-specific

