## Engine Upgrade Checklist (for future releases)

When building a new engine release via `release-engine.sh`:

1. Download `wine-devel-{VERSION}-osx64.tar.xz` from Gcenx/macOS_Wine_builds
2. Download DXMT builtin variant from 3Shain/dxmt
3. Download VKD3D-proton from `HansKristian-Work/vkd3d-proton` — place at `wine/lib/vkd3d-proton/x86_64-windows/`
4. Download DXVK from doitsujin/dxvk
5. Run `wineboot --init` to build prefix template
6. Validate: wine64 --version, NLS files, DXMT files, VKD3D-proton d3d12.dll, prefix template
7. Tag as vX.Y.Z-engine and publish to GitHub Releases

**DXMT must be version-compatible with Wine:** DXMT's `wiremetal.so` links to `wiremac.so` and requires the macdrv Metal APIs (added in Wine 10.x). Using DXMT built against Wine 11.x with Wine 8.x causes "Failed to create metal view" crash.

**VKD3D-proton DLLs are installed into prefix system32 at runtime** (not bundled in the Wine lib directory) — `WinePrefix.installVKD3DProton` handles this. The engine package ships them at `wine/lib/vkd3d-proton/x86_64-windows/`.

